'''''Berula''''' is a cosmopolitan genus of [[flowering plant]]s in the family [[Apiaceae]], whose species are known as '''water parsnips''',<ref name=calflora>[https://www.calflora.org/cgi-bin/species_query.cgi?where-calrecnum=1081 Calflora taxon report, University of California: ''Berula erecta'']</ref> as are some other plants in Apiaceae such as ''[[Sium latifolium]]'' and ''[[Sium suave]]''.  It is easily confused with the highly toxic [[water hemlock]] (''Cicuta maculata''). 

''Berula'' species are perennial, aquatic to semi-aquatic, herbaceous plants. The leaves are usually oppositely arranged. The flowerheads are arranged in [[umbel]]s of small white flowers. ''[[Berula erecta]]'' is a widespread [[aquatic plant]] with fern-like leaves, found across Eurasia, Africa, North America, and elsewhere.<ref name=calflora/><ref name=foc>{{eFloras|2|103870|volume=14|Berula |last1=Fading |first1=Pu |last2=Watson |first2=Mark F. |accessdate=16 December 2018}}</ref>

